WEBVTT

1
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:23.080
I am a stone.

2
00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.880
I do not move.

3
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.200
Very slowly,
I put snow in my mouth,

4
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.200
then he won't
see my breath.

5
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.720
I take my time.
I let him come closer.

6
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.400
I have only one bullet.
I am at his eye.

7
00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.600
Very gently, my finger
presses on the trigger.

8
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.240
I do not tremble.

9
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.560
I have no fear.
I'm a big boy now.

10
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.360
Ready, Vassili?

11
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.080
Now, Vassili.
Fire!

12
00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.200
Fire, Vassili!
Fire!

13
00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.680
- Come on, pick your feet up.

14
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.040
Get on your feet.
Prepare to board the train.

15
00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.040
You there, come along with me now.
This way, pal.

16
00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.520
All civilians, get out!

17
00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.960
Make way, let the civilians off.

18
00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.240
This is a military convoy.

19
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:54.760
No one stays on board
but our valiant soldiers.

20
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.280
This is a convoy
to Stalingrad...

21
00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.680
only for the soldiers
of the Red Army.

22
00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.400
All aboard!

23
00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.400
Autumn, 1942.

24
00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:53.800
Europe lies crushed
beneath the Nazi jackboot.

25
00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:00.280
The German Third Reich
is at the height of its power.

26
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.600
Hitler's armies are charging
through the heart of the Soviet Union...

27
00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.040
towards the oil fields
of Asia.

28
00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:09.520
One last obstacle remains.
A city on the Volga...

29
00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:13.520
where the fate of the world
is being decided: Stalingrad.

30
00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.480
Glorious comrade Stalin...

31
00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.240
has ordered not another
step backwards.

32
00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.320
The people of the Soviet Union
shall be free.

33
00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.000
Go forward, comrades.
Not a step backwards!

34
00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.160
Listen to these letters
sent by Russian mothers...

35
00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.240
to their sons on the front.

36
00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:57.240
"Volodya, my child,
I know that it's for our motherland -

37
00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:05.880
"l know that it's for our motherland
that you are giving your life.

38
00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:24.920
"Everyone here knows
that you will not fall back.

39
00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.920
"Everyone here
is proud of you.

40
00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:33.360
"Your father is dead.
Your brothers are dead.

41
00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.880
Avenge us
on the hordes off ascists. "

42
00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.480
Nobody move!
Stay on the boat!

43
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.560
- Get back or I'll shoot!

44
00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.880
Back from the rails, or we shoot.
Shoot the traitors!

45
00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.520
Come on, come on!
Move!

46
00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:03.640
Come on, comrades,
come on!

47
00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.560
Move, or you'll be shot!

48
00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:24.280
Over here, stretcher!

49
00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.360
The one with
the rifle shoots!

50
00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.000
One out of two
gets a rifle.

51
00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.280
The one without
follows him!

52
00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:40.840
When the one
with the rifle gets killed,

53
00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:45.480
the one who is following
picks up the rifle and shoots!

54
00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:50.560
The one with
the rifle shoots!

55
00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:53.880
The one without follows him!

56
00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.520
When the one with
the rifle gets killed,

57
00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.000
the one who is following...

58
00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.920
picks up the rifle and shoots!

59
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.920
The one with
the rifle shoots!

60
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.760
- This way, now.
- The one without follows him!

61
00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.880
Soldiers of the glorious
Red Army, from now on...

62
00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:40.200
it is either victory
or death!

63
00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:44.120
- Those who retreat will be shot.
- I need a rifle.

64
00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.640
There will be no mercy
for cowards and traitors!

65
00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.680
Achtung!

66
00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.680
Aah!

67
00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:36.200
It's hopeless, comrades.
Get back!

68
00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.760
Pull back!

69
00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.520
Pull back!

70
00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.360
Get back! Get back!

71
00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:48.240
In the name
of the Soviet Union,

72
00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:51.000
not a step backwards,
or we shoot.

73
00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.200
No retreat!
Not a step back!

74
00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:57.160
- No mercy!
- Deserters will be shot.

75
00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.720
- Fire!
- Shoot the traitors!

76
00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.320
Cowards will be shot!

77
00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.560
No mercy for cowards!

78
00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:46.760
Russians, surrender.
You will see your home again.

79
00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.400
This is not your war.

80
00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.720
Join your German comrades,
they under stand your suffering...

81
00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.520
and will care more for you
than your own officers,

82
00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.760
who are only sending you
to your death.

83
00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.200
The Third Reich
is not your enemy.

84
00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:07.720
The enemy is blood thirsty Stalin
and his Bolshevik camp,

85
00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:11.280
who have stolen your land, who have
deported your father-

86
00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:34.800
Fire!

87
00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:32.120
You'll get us caught,
comrade Commissar.

88
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:55.400
With your permission,
comrade Commissar.

89
00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:30.000
- Which one should I aim at first?
- You should wait...

90
00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:31.960
till there's an explosion.

91
00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:47.800
- Do you know how to shoot?
- A little.

92
00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:39.600
Don't shoot. Don't shoot.
He's looking at us.

93
00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.800
Thank you,
comrade Commissar.

94
00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:55.920
Danilov, political officer,
second class.

95
00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:59.760
Twenty-first infantry.

96
00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:20.640
"Vassili Zaitsev. "

97
00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.920
"On this day,
September the 20th, 1942,

98
00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:26.520
- "a shepherd boy from the Urals...

99
00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:33.120
"arrived in the city of Stalingrad,
on the banks of the Volga.

100
00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:35.880
"His name is Vassili Zaitsev.

101
00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:41.480
"Like thousands before him, he came
to answer comrade Stalin's call.

102
00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:46.880
"Armed with a rifle, he quickly made
the fascist invader realize that...

103
00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:51.880
"from now on he would be punished for
every step he took in the motherland;

104
00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:55.120
that from here on,
the only way was back. "

105
00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.880
What do you think?

106
00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:04.520
I think comrade Commissar's
been overgenerous.

107
00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:24.840
Let me go!
Let me go!

108
00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:33.040
By order of comrade Stalin,
no civilian can leave the city.

109
00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.760
- Get back!

110
00:21:38.840 --> 00:21:41.200
Stand away,
or we will open fire.

111
00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:53.760
- Stand away!

112
00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:55.720
Get back!

113
00:21:56.720 --> 00:21:58.560
Get back or we shoot!

114
00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:00.200
Back!
Keep back!

115
00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:04.560
Make way for
comrade Stalin 's envoy!

116
00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:11.160
I carried out my orders.

117
00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:14.360
I sent in
all of my boys.

118
00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:17.840
But the Germans
engulfed us.

119
00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:21.920
They have artillery,
aircraft, tanks.

120
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:26.000
- And me, what did I have?
- The sacred duty to resist!

121
00:22:26.040 --> 00:22:28.400
I have to
report to the boss.

122
00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:33.480
Perhaps you'd prefer
to avoid the red tape.

123
00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:58.000
My name is...

124
00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:02.560
Nikita Sergeyevich Kruschev.

125
00:23:03.840 --> 00:23:06.480
I've come to take things
in hand here.

126
00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:10.400
This city is not Kursk...

127
00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:14.160
nor is it Kiev, nor Minsk.

128
00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:17.640
This city is Stalingrad.

129
00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:21.280
Stalingrad!

130
00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:24.400
This city bears the name
of the boss.

131
00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:26.960
It's more than a city,
it's a symbol.

132
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:32.040
If the Germans
capture this city,

133
00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:36.360
the entire country
will collapse.

134
00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:40.440
Now, I want our boys...

135
00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:43.040
to raise their heads.

136
00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:46.640
I want them to act like
they have balls!

137
00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:50.680
I want them to stop shitting
their pants!

138
00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:57.360
That's your job.

139
00:23:57.400 --> 00:24:02.520
As political officers,
I'm counting on you.

140
00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:08.800
You,
what's your suggestion?

141
00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:11.200
Shoot all the other generals
who have retreated...

142
00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:14.320
and their
chiefs of staff too.

143
00:24:14.400 --> 00:24:17.120
M-Make some examples.

144
00:24:17.200 --> 00:24:21.280
-D-D-Deport families of the deserters-
-Yeah, that's all been done.

145
00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:23.640
Give them hope!

146
00:24:34.960 --> 00:24:38.920
Here, the men's only choice
is between German bullets and ours.

147
00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.960
But there's another way.
The way of courage.

148
00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:44.360
The way of love
of the motherland.

149
00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:46.280
We must publish
the army newspaper again.

150
00:24:46.360 --> 00:24:48.360
We must tell magnificent stories.
Stories that extol...

151
00:24:48.440 --> 00:24:50.320
sacrifice, bravery.

152
00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:52.600
We must make them believe
in the victory.

153
00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:56.520
We must give them hope,
pride, a desire to fight.

154
00:24:56.600 --> 00:25:00.520
Yes, we need to
make examples.

155
00:25:00.600 --> 00:25:03.600
But examples to follow.

156
00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:07.360
What we need...
are heroes.

157
00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:13.520
Do you know any heroes
around here?

158
00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:18.800
Yes, comrade,
I know one.

159
00:25:23.360 --> 00:25:25.440
That's me!

160
00:25:25.520 --> 00:25:29.320
"Vassili Zaitsev. "
That's me!

161
00:25:29.400 --> 00:25:32.320
No, you're not dreaming.
It's your name.

162
00:25:32.400 --> 00:25:35.040
We made the front page.

163
00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:38.240
They haven't changed a word.

164
00:25:38.320 --> 00:25:41.560
Do you have any idea
what this means?

165
00:25:41.640 --> 00:25:44.120
It's not the back page,
it's not the second page,

166
00:25:44.160 --> 00:25:46.360
- it's the front page.
- The front page!

167
00:25:46.400 --> 00:25:48.720
They're going to reprint
our article everywhere.

168
00:25:48.800 --> 00:25:52.600
In the Caucasus, in the Crimea,
even in the Urals.

169
00:25:52.680 --> 00:25:55.920
Tomorrow morning, Stalin himself
will be sitting over breakfast,

170
00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:59.560
reading my words,
memorizing your name.

171
00:25:59.640 --> 00:26:02.200
We're famous, Vassili.
Kruschev loved the article.

172
00:26:02.280 --> 00:26:04.280
He's promoted me
to the general staff.

173
00:26:04.320 --> 00:26:07.680
And you
to sniper division.

174
00:26:09.760 --> 00:26:11.640
- Well, that's good.
- It's very good.

175
00:26:11.680 --> 00:26:14.760
- It's very good. It's great.
- It's very great!

176
00:26:14.840 --> 00:26:16.960
- It's great!
- For us because we did it together.

177
00:26:17.040 --> 00:26:18.480
- Together!

178
00:26:18.560 --> 00:26:20.520
- Although I did all the hard work.
- Oh, yeah?

179
00:26:20.600 --> 00:26:22.840
- You're very lucky I can't fight back.
- Why's that?

180
00:26:22.880 --> 00:26:25.120
Because Kruschev told me to make sure
nothing happens to you.

181
00:26:25.200 --> 00:26:27.120
- You're too important.
- I'm too valuable.

182
00:26:27.200 --> 00:26:29.600
Yes, careful of my- careful
of my glasses, please. They're new.

183
00:26:29.680 --> 00:26:31.600
Sorry, sir.

184
00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:36.000
- I'm famous! We're famous!
- I'm famous! I'm famous!

185
00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:38.520
Vassili,
the young shepherd from the Urals,

186
00:26:38.600 --> 00:26:40.480
killed his 12th
German officer today.

187
00:26:40.520 --> 00:26:42.440
He used to hunt wolves,
now he shoots fascists.

188
00:26:42.520 --> 00:26:45.520
Today, Vassili Zaitsev
shot his 23rd German officer.

189
00:26:45.600 --> 00:26:47.480
He is an example to us all.

190
00:26:47.560 --> 00:26:50.040
Vassilis hot
his 32nd German officer.

191
00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:56.480
Count only the Germans
you have killed.

192
00:26:56.520 --> 00:26:58.440
- Today, Vassili Zaitsev-
- Here is the evidence-

193
00:26:58.520 --> 00:27:01.080
11 dog tags retrieved
by sniper Vassili Zaitsev.

194
00:27:06.480 --> 00:27:09.520
More and more men and women, fighters
from all branches of our armed forces,

195
00:27:09.600 --> 00:27:13.840
join the sniper division and learn
the skills of Vassili Zaitsev.

196
00:27:17.760 --> 00:27:19.680
I am a stone.

197
00:27:23.200 --> 00:27:25.560
I am a stone.

198
00:27:26.640 --> 00:27:28.560
I breathe slowly.

199
00:27:36.160 --> 00:27:39.000
I am at the eye.

200
00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:09.080
So it is you,

201
00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:12.640
the great Vassili Zaitsev.

202
00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:16.080
- My mother makes potatoes with bacon.
- Sounds good.

203
00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.520
When she sees you,
she won't believe her eyes.

204
00:28:20.360 --> 00:28:24.600
- How many today?
- Only two.

205
00:28:24.680 --> 00:28:27.360
And the last one,
why didn't you shoot him?

206
00:28:27.440 --> 00:28:31.960
He was only a foot soldier.
Wasn't worth giving away my position.

207
00:28:32.040 --> 00:28:36.080
- Bless you.

208
00:28:37.320 --> 00:28:37.960
We know how much
we owe you.

209
00:28:38.040 --> 00:28:41.400
We pray for you every day.

210
00:28:41.480 --> 00:28:46.080
Every evening, we listen to them talk
about you on Radio Moscow.

211
00:28:46.160 --> 00:28:49.680
Thanks. You've certainly
managed well down here.

212
00:28:49.760 --> 00:28:54.200
My parents used to store furniture
down here before the war.

213
00:28:54.280 --> 00:28:56.840
Sacha, drop that right now.

214
00:28:56.880 --> 00:28:59.760
It's loaded.

215
00:29:07.880 --> 00:29:09.720
This way, comrade Commissar.

216
00:29:09.800 --> 00:29:11.720
Thank you, comrade.

217
00:29:13.440 --> 00:29:15.680
Good evening.

218
00:29:18.040 --> 00:29:20.440
Comrade Zaitsev?

219
00:29:23.480 --> 00:29:28.280
My God, where does
all this mail come from?

220
00:29:28.360 --> 00:29:33.200
From all over the country,
Mrs. Filipov, from all over.

221
00:29:33.280 --> 00:29:35.240
This one's from the workers
of the Kouzbass.

222
00:29:35.320 --> 00:29:38.200
They want to name
their mine after Vassili.

223
00:29:38.280 --> 00:29:40.200
Right, let's start
with the miners.

224
00:29:41.560 --> 00:29:44.040
Come on,
let's get to work.

225
00:29:48.200 --> 00:29:50.680
Dear comrades
from the Kouzbass,

226
00:29:50.760 --> 00:29:54.600
- Kouzbass.
- I thank you for your letter of praise.

227
00:29:54.640 --> 00:29:57.360
- Praise?
- R-A-l-S-E.

228
00:29:59.920 --> 00:30:04.920
And... I hope that
I can live up...

229
00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:09.720
to your expectations-
A-T-l-O-N-S.

230
00:30:09.800 --> 00:30:13.360
Expectations.

231
00:30:13.440 --> 00:30:16.120
You're interested
in German literature, Mrs. Filipov?

232
00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:22.000
It's all right,
it's our neighbor.

233
00:30:22.040 --> 00:30:24.520
- Right, where were we?
- Tania, we have guests.

234
00:30:24.560 --> 00:30:27.280
Your offer to name-

235
00:30:33.880 --> 00:30:36.920
I-

236
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:38.840
I-l recognize you.

237
00:30:41.560 --> 00:30:43.400
He's Vassili Zaitsev.

238
00:30:46.760 --> 00:30:49.200
I saw your picture
in the paper.

239
00:30:49.280 --> 00:30:52.200
Thank you
for every thing you're doing.

240
00:30:52.280 --> 00:30:55.800
- And this is his friend, Commissar...
- Danilov.

241
00:30:55.880 --> 00:30:57.920
Danilov.

242
00:30:58.000 --> 00:31:00.000
Tania is like
a daughter to me.

243
00:31:00.080 --> 00:31:03.280
She used to take care of Sacha
when I worked at the factory.

244
00:31:03.320 --> 00:31:05.400
She even taught him German.
All these books are hers.

245
00:31:05.480 --> 00:31:08.960
- Oh, they're yours?
- She studied German at the university.

246
00:31:09.040 --> 00:31:11.240
- Which university?
- Moscow.

247
00:31:16.240 --> 00:31:19.480
Moscow. Moscow.

248
00:31:21.480 --> 00:31:23.560
Shouldn't we, uh-

249
00:31:23.640 --> 00:31:26.760
Yes, let's continue.

250
00:31:26.840 --> 00:31:31.080
Your offer to name
your mine after me...

251
00:31:31.160 --> 00:31:34.640
is... a great honor.

252
00:31:36.280 --> 00:31:40.160
H-O-N.

253
00:31:40.240 --> 00:31:42.160
Yes, I know.
Honor.

254
00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:44.800
Very good.

255
00:31:44.880 --> 00:31:50.080
Shouldn't we make the point that
I'm not the only one fighting?

256
00:31:50.160 --> 00:31:54.000
That- That's excellent-
excellent idea, Vassili.

257
00:31:54.040 --> 00:31:56.040
- We can take it even further though.
- Oh.

258
00:31:56.120 --> 00:31:57.960
We can take it further.

259
00:31:58.040 --> 00:32:01.920
Your battle for
the production of coal...

260
00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:05.440
is as worthy as mine.

261
00:32:05.520 --> 00:32:10.160
There's no "K" in coal.

262
00:32:10.200 --> 00:32:12.120
Just-just one "L"

263
00:32:14.520 --> 00:32:17.360
Oh, tell me if I'm going too fast.

264
00:32:17.400 --> 00:32:20.080
- No, you're not going too fast.
- You sure?

265
00:32:20.120 --> 00:32:22.160
I just thought is there
any other improvements?

266
00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:26.520
Why don't you get some rest?
These letters can wait until tomorrow.

267
00:32:26.600 --> 00:32:28.920
We should carry on.
We're not tired.

268
00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:32.040
Thank you, Mrs. Filipov.
These people...

269
00:32:32.120 --> 00:32:34.840
took the trouble
to write to us.

270
00:32:34.920 --> 00:32:38.120
Tomorrow, we may not
be around to write back.

271
00:33:46.680 --> 00:33:48.560
Major Konig,
Herr General.

272
00:34:08.400 --> 00:34:11.760
I was expecting
someone...

273
00:34:11.840 --> 00:34:13.680
else.

274
00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:16.480
Certainly not someone
so prestigious.

275
00:34:16.560 --> 00:34:18.480
I imagine you have
your reasons...

276
00:34:18.560 --> 00:34:22.240
for getting your self involved
in this hellish situation.

277
00:34:25.240 --> 00:34:28.960
My army is not designed
for this kind of fighting.

278
00:34:29.040 --> 00:34:31.160
Yesterday, yet again,
I had to promote...

279
00:34:31.240 --> 00:34:35.560
25 sergeants to replace the officers
shot down by their sharp shooters.

280
00:34:37.320 --> 00:34:40.960
Those snipers are
demoralizing my people.

281
00:34:41.040 --> 00:34:45.200
This city is no more than...

282
00:34:45.280 --> 00:34:47.200
a heap of ruins.

283
00:34:49.160 --> 00:34:52.240
But the fuehrer's persisting.

284
00:34:52.320 --> 00:34:55.360
He has made it a personal matter
between Stalin and himself.

285
00:35:01.320 --> 00:35:04.800
We should trust
the fuehrer's instinct.

286
00:35:04.880 --> 00:35:08.360
He always managed to
lead us to victory.

287
00:35:10.160 --> 00:35:13.840
We shall be back home
for Christmas.

288
00:35:16.320 --> 00:35:20.240
How are you going to go about finding
this young Russian?

289
00:35:20.320 --> 00:35:26.000
I'll fix it so that he's the one
who finds me.

290
00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:29.920
Vassili.
Vassili.

291
00:35:29.960 --> 00:35:32.920
- Come on, time to get up.
- What?

292
00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:36.640
They have a problem in the department
store sector. They need us. Come on.

293
00:35:45.880 --> 00:35:49.400
Look, Vassili, he's hiding
in the department store. Over there.

294
00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:56.040
So far this morning,

295
00:35:56.120 --> 00:36:00.280
he's knocked off five officers,
plus two machine gunners.

296
00:36:02.320 --> 00:36:07.040
Look, third floor,
fourth window from the left.

297
00:36:07.120 --> 00:36:10.720
Fourth window from the left.

298
00:36:13.360 --> 00:36:15.200
See him?

299
00:36:15.280 --> 00:36:17.840
Yeah, I see him.

300
00:36:28.920 --> 00:36:31.720
There, you got him!

301
00:36:31.760 --> 00:36:34.480
Great shot.

302
00:36:36.800 --> 00:36:39.560
Let's go get
his dog tag.

303
00:36:43.280 --> 00:36:45.360
Good-bye, comrade Commissar.

304
00:36:45.440 --> 00:36:48.000
Thank you for your
hospitality, Mrs. Filipov.

305
00:36:55.880 --> 00:36:58.800
You can borrow
whatever you like.

306
00:36:58.880 --> 00:37:01.440
I'm not sure what they would say
to me at headquarters...

307
00:37:01.520 --> 00:37:04.360
if I came back with an armful
of Goethe and Schiller.

308
00:37:04.400 --> 00:37:06.400
- There's some Marx too.

309
00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:10.000
You were assigned to civil defense
at the 12th district?

310
00:37:10.080 --> 00:37:12.200
No, I volunteered.

311
00:37:12.280 --> 00:37:15.360
It's such a coincidence
meeting you like this.

312
00:37:15.440 --> 00:37:17.360
Comrade Kruschev was
telling me just yesterday...

313
00:37:17.440 --> 00:37:19.720
how desperately we're in need
of operators who speak German.

314
00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:23.440
I can't. Our militia's responsible
for all the people in this neighborhood.

315
00:37:23.520 --> 00:37:25.440
We're already
desperately short of men.

316
00:37:25.480 --> 00:37:28.360
We'll give you a dozen soldiers
for every one that speaks German.

317
00:37:28.440 --> 00:37:30.280
I'd rather stay and fight.

318
00:37:30.360 --> 00:37:33.360
Serving at headquarters is fighting.
You'd be far more useful there.

319
00:37:35.680 --> 00:37:37.720
You stay here.
You cover us.

320
00:37:37.800 --> 00:37:39.840
- All right.
- We go.

321
00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:44.360
Take care.

322
00:37:47.840 --> 00:37:49.680
Ludmilla, come on.

323
00:38:39.600 --> 00:38:41.520
Check the stairway.

324
00:40:25.920 --> 00:40:27.800
It's a trap.

325
00:40:27.840 --> 00:40:30.080
I know.

326
00:40:52.520 --> 00:40:55.360
Move back.

327
00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:43.520
He's still here.

328
00:42:07.320 --> 00:42:09.800
- They're coming straight for us!
- Ludmilla,

329
00:42:09.880 --> 00:42:13.480
stay where you are,
he's over there somewhere.

330
00:42:24.080 --> 00:42:26.240
We have to
get out of here!

331
00:42:29.240 --> 00:42:32.440
- We have to get out of here!
-Just stay where you are!

332
00:42:35.920 --> 00:42:37.800
What are we gonna do?

333
00:42:37.880 --> 00:42:40.160
Ludmilla, stay where you are!

334
00:42:50.680 --> 00:42:53.280
Fuck this, I'm going.

335
00:42:55.080 --> 00:42:58.080
Ludmilla, no!

336
00:43:47.240 --> 00:43:49.000
What does this mean?

337
00:43:51.280 --> 00:43:54.280
"The little shepherd from the Urals
receives a new sniper's rifle,

338
00:43:54.360 --> 00:43:59.880
"a Mosin-Nagant 7. 62,
with its 3. 5-power P. U. telescope.

339
00:43:59.960 --> 00:44:01.880
Pride of precision
of Soviet production. "

340
00:44:01.960 --> 00:44:05.160
- I've seen that rifle close up.
- Have you?

341
00:44:05.240 --> 00:44:09.800
I've even touched it.
I know him well, Vassili Zaitsev.

342
00:44:57.160 --> 00:45:01.640
Ludmilla and Anton were killed today,
and it was my fault.

343
00:45:01.720 --> 00:45:04.040
No, I'm sure
that's not true.

344
00:45:04.120 --> 00:45:09.280
There was a German sniper.
I walked them right into his trap.

345
00:45:09.320 --> 00:45:12.600
- What else can you tell me?
- He didn 't relocate.

346
00:45:12.680 --> 00:45:17.320
A sniper who doesn't
relocate isn't normal.

347
00:45:18.840 --> 00:45:24.560
He was very good. It wasn't just
his shooting, it was his instinct.

348
00:45:24.600 --> 00:45:27.160
He was a step ahead
of me all the time.

349
00:45:27.240 --> 00:45:31.200
That's because he knows
everything about you.

350
00:45:31.280 --> 00:45:34.040
His name is Konig,
Major Konig.

351
00:45:34.120 --> 00:45:38.600
They've sent him here
to ki-

352
00:45:38.640 --> 00:45:41.640
to find you.

353
00:45:47.760 --> 00:45:50.440
At first we weren't sure
if the information was reliable.

354
00:45:50.480 --> 00:45:53.400
It seems he's come
all the way from Berlin to stop you.

355
00:45:53.480 --> 00:45:56.800
You've caused them so many sleepless
nights, they sent their top marksman.

356
00:45:56.880 --> 00:46:00.680
- What do we know about him?
- He's a major in the Wehrmacht.

357
00:46:00.760 --> 00:46:04.600
He's director of their
sniper school in Zossen.

358
00:46:04.680 --> 00:46:08.000
Koulikov studied under him
at Zossen before the war.

359
00:46:08.080 --> 00:46:12.280
He knows all his tricks. From no won,
he'll go with you everywhere.

360
00:46:12.360 --> 00:46:15.640
A nobleman from Bavaria
who hunts deer...

361
00:46:15.720 --> 00:46:18.760
against a shepherd boy from the Urals
who poaches wolves.

362
00:46:18.840 --> 00:46:21.680
It's more than a confrontation
between two nations.

363
00:46:25.000 --> 00:46:28.040
It's the essence
of class struggle.

364
00:46:28.080 --> 00:46:30.640
I'm glad
you're so happy.

365
00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:35.680
He had all the advantages.
Next time you'll be even.

366
00:46:35.760 --> 00:46:38.360
No one shoots
like you, Vassili.

367
00:46:46.920 --> 00:46:49.800
She's been transferred.

368
00:46:49.840 --> 00:46:53.200
I'll see if they're ready
for you next door.

369
00:46:57.800 --> 00:47:00.920
- Hello.
- You look smart in your new uniform.

370
00:47:02.320 --> 00:47:05.200
Make sure they don't take it back
once you've finished.

371
00:47:05.280 --> 00:47:07.520
Yeah, they probably will.

372
00:47:11.120 --> 00:47:15.360
I've heard the rumor about the German,
and I wanted to wish you luck.

373
00:47:15.440 --> 00:47:17.880
Thank you.
I'll need it.

374
00:47:17.960 --> 00:47:22.440
From what comrade Danilov
tells me, you're going to win.

375
00:47:24.360 --> 00:47:27.040
Hmm.

376
00:47:27.120 --> 00:47:29.160
It's time.

377
00:47:29.200 --> 00:47:31.680
@@@@@@

378
00:47:31.760 --> 00:47:34.560
- Vassili! Vassili!
- Come to my arms.

379
00:47:35.880 --> 00:47:39.640
- Look in my direction.

380
00:47:39.720 --> 00:47:41.880
Put your cap back on,
you look more heroic.

381
00:47:41.960 --> 00:47:44.680
- This way, comrade Zaitsev.
- I love this little fellow.

382
00:47:44.720 --> 00:47:48.120
Vassili, is it true that
you volunteered for the front?

383
00:47:48.240 --> 00:47:49.120
How old are you, Vassili?

384
00:47:49.160 --> 00:47:51.080
Do you know what this duel
means for our country?

385
00:47:51.160 --> 00:47:54.920
Is it true you killed your first wolf
when you were five?

386
00:47:54.960 --> 00:47:57.560
Are you proud to be challenged
by the best sharp shooter in Germany?

387
00:47:57.640 --> 00:47:59.520
The Germans are starting
to shit their pants.

388
00:47:59.600 --> 00:48:02.680
Go on, my boy, tell us how
you're going to deal with him.

389
00:48:02.760 --> 00:48:06.040
- Or rather, no. Tell it to the boss.
- One more question, please.

390
00:48:06.120 --> 00:48:09.160
He likes
good hunting stories.

391
00:48:14.480 --> 00:48:17.520
Look at him with pride,

392
00:48:17.600 --> 00:48:20.240
because he's looking at you.

393
00:48:20.320 --> 00:48:23.960
The whole country
is looking at you.

394
00:48:44.520 --> 00:48:48.800
Forgive me, forgive me,
Grandfather.

395
00:49:19.440 --> 00:49:22.400
So, it's not the wolf that
chooses the hunting ground...

396
00:49:22.440 --> 00:49:24.680
but the hunter.

397
00:49:28.200 --> 00:49:31.080
But I'm sure your grandfather
taught you that.

398
00:49:35.040 --> 00:49:37.240
Except in this case,

399
00:49:37.320 --> 00:49:39.160
I'm the game.

400
00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:46.120
However,
today what we're going to do...

401
00:49:46.160 --> 00:49:48.480
is lure the wolf
out of his lair...

402
00:49:48.560 --> 00:49:51.520
to where we want him to be.

403
00:50:28.720 --> 00:50:32.040
You're the one whose life is valuable.
You go first.

404
00:50:32.080 --> 00:50:36.600
No, no. We take it in turns.
Next time is your turn to go first,

405
00:50:36.680 --> 00:50:38.560
and then it's you, Volodya.

406
00:50:53.000 --> 00:50:57.080
Son of a bitch!

407
00:50:59.800 --> 00:51:04.320
These are new pants. I just took them
off a captain from the 251st yesterday.

408
00:51:08.040 --> 00:51:12.360
Sixteen months I spent
in Germany at the school in Zossen.

409
00:51:12.400 --> 00:51:16.160
Of course, those were the days
when we were friends with the Krauts:

410
00:51:16.240 --> 00:51:19.520
when our Joseph
and their Adolph...

411
00:51:19.600 --> 00:51:22.520
were walking hand in hand.

412
00:51:24.200 --> 00:51:27.000
From here to the wire,
160meters, right?

413
00:51:32.560 --> 00:51:34.440
One hundred and fifty-five.

414
00:51:34.520 --> 00:51:39.040
Whatever. That'll make 'em
send out a repair guy.

415
00:51:39.120 --> 00:51:42.280
Let's relocate.

416
00:51:48.600 --> 00:51:50.360
Aah!

417
00:52:01.120 --> 00:52:03.200
Hey, Volodya!

418
00:52:12.280 --> 00:52:15.200
After the Germans
invaded us,

419
00:52:15.280 --> 00:52:19.120
it wasn't the same
atmosphere anymore.

420
00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:21.640
Threw my ass
in prison.

421
00:52:21.720 --> 00:52:24.400
What were you doing
in Germany, huh?

422
00:52:24.440 --> 00:52:28.920
Excuse me, says I, but it was
comrade Stalin who sent me there.

423
00:52:29.000 --> 00:52:33.520
Don't bring our glorious leader
into your treachery.

424
00:52:33.560 --> 00:52:36.880
Confess, spy bastard!
Confess.

425
00:52:36.920 --> 00:52:40.760
And bang! Bang, bang, bang!

426
00:52:43.960 --> 00:52:46.600
Well, there wasn't a sickle,
but there was a hammer.

427
00:52:46.680 --> 00:52:50.960
And bang.
Knocked out all my teeth.

428
00:52:53.280 --> 00:52:57.240
That's right, boy.
Have no illusions.

429
00:52:57.320 --> 00:53:00.520
That's the land of socialism
and universal bliss for you.

430
00:53:03.720 --> 00:53:08.200
Hey! It's your repair guy.

431
00:53:08.280 --> 00:53:10.640
I got him.

432
00:53:23.920 --> 00:53:25.760
It's about soup time,
isn't it?

433
00:53:25.840 --> 00:53:28.560
I'm going.

434
00:53:28.600 --> 00:53:31.320
Well, get a move on, Volodya,

435
00:53:31.400 --> 00:53:36.800
and try not to spill it all
on your way back, you Marxist bastard.

436
00:53:48.480 --> 00:53:52.080
The enemy sniper activity reported
during the past 24 hours, Herr Major.

437
00:53:54.480 --> 00:53:58.040
Two sentries shot
in the train station sector.

438
00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:00.920
One artillery observer
in the Northern sector.

439
00:54:00.960 --> 00:54:04.200
One lieutenant from the 24th Panzer
division in the factory sector.

440
00:54:04.280 --> 00:54:07.640
Three telephone repairmen
in the workers' housing sector.

441
00:54:07.720 --> 00:54:11.840
They also tell me we have just taken
a prisoner who may interest you.

442
00:54:11.920 --> 00:54:13.760
I hope he's still
able to speak.

443
00:54:13.840 --> 00:54:16.360
Excuse me, sir?

444
00:54:16.440 --> 00:54:18.840
Nothing.
Thank you.

445
00:54:24.320 --> 00:54:26.360
which building is he in?

446
00:54:29.040 --> 00:54:30.880
There is no way
I know that.

447
00:54:33.200 --> 00:54:35.120
He moves around
all the time.

448
00:54:35.200 --> 00:54:38.000
He jumps from one
to the next.

449
00:54:38.080 --> 00:54:39.920
On which floor?

450
00:54:40.000 --> 00:54:41.840
I don't know.

451
00:54:41.920 --> 00:54:44.920
We'll see about that.

452
00:54:45.000 --> 00:54:47.360
Undress him.

453
00:54:47.440 --> 00:54:49.800
Put him in
one of our uniforms.

454
00:55:17.080 --> 00:55:20.160
You see, they are stubborn.

455
00:55:20.240 --> 00:55:22.320
That's the good thing
about the Germans.

456
00:55:22.400 --> 00:55:26.560
Man, you got to admit
when they get an idea in their heads-

457
00:55:41.840 --> 00:55:43.880
Right.

458
00:55:43.960 --> 00:55:46.280
Let's see if our customer
has arrived.

459
00:55:46.360 --> 00:55:48.760
Are you ready?

460
00:55:48.840 --> 00:55:50.680
Uh-huh.

461
00:55:50.760 --> 00:55:54.800
And now our famous shepherd
from the Urals,

462
00:55:54.880 --> 00:55:57.080
who Major Konig
thinks is an idiot,

463
00:55:57.160 --> 00:56:00.000
gets up to make sure
he has hit his target.

464
00:56:00.080 --> 00:56:02.760
Major Konig sees him.

465
00:56:06.120 --> 00:56:08.800
Aims for his helmet.

466
00:56:08.880 --> 00:56:11.320
Fires.

467
00:56:11.400 --> 00:56:14.560
Reveals his position
and is shot in turn.

468
00:56:25.120 --> 00:56:29.120
Except...
Major Konig doesn't fire...

469
00:56:32.520 --> 00:56:35.240
because Major Konig
isn't there.

470
00:56:39.040 --> 00:56:40.920
Koulikov!

471
00:56:46.360 --> 00:56:49.840
Don't you think that was strange,
that last one?

472
00:56:49.920 --> 00:56:52.920
They sent him out
to get shot like the others.

473
00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:54.840
It's not natural.

474
00:56:54.920 --> 00:56:58.240
Not without artillery,
without trying to cover him.

475
00:57:00.240 --> 00:57:03.280
Oh, no, I'm the one
who was stupid.

476
00:57:03.360 --> 00:57:05.520
They don't give a shit
about telephone guys.

477
00:57:05.560 --> 00:57:07.440
I mean, it's like us
with the Ukrainians.

478
00:57:07.480 --> 00:57:10.840
They'd never bother a major
over a few dead grunts.

479
00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:16.480
Tomorrow, we'll kill us
some generals.

480
00:57:24.640 --> 00:57:27.240
Whose turn is it?

481
00:57:27.320 --> 00:57:30.040
Mine, I think.

482
00:57:30.080 --> 00:57:32.280
Oh, you're such a cheater!

483
00:57:33.600 --> 00:57:35.600
You can't fool Papa Koulikov.

484
00:57:35.680 --> 00:57:39.400
No, no, no, no, no, no, no,
it's my turn to go first.

485
00:57:41.400 --> 00:57:44.400
And it's your turn to get a hole
in your britches.

486
00:58:57.480 --> 00:58:59.320
To victory.

487
00:59:06.440 --> 00:59:10.960
This sniper business
has been dragging on too long.

488
00:59:11.040 --> 00:59:13.200
What's that little fellow
of yours up to?

489
00:59:15.960 --> 00:59:18.320
He's probing,
comrade Kruschev.

490
00:59:18.400 --> 00:59:20.760
He's testing the Germans
for weaknesses.

491
00:59:20.840 --> 00:59:22.680
He's meticulous
in his preparation.

492
00:59:25.000 --> 00:59:29.720
Vodka...
is a luxury we have.

493
00:59:29.800 --> 00:59:33.040
Caviar is
a luxury we have.

494
00:59:33.120 --> 00:59:35.880
Time is not.

495
00:59:35.920 --> 00:59:38.760
He's aware of that
comrade Kruschev. We both are.

496
00:59:40.960 --> 00:59:43.080
I assure you
he will succeed.

497
00:59:43.160 --> 00:59:45.120
Good.

498
00:59:45.200 --> 00:59:49.280
It seems your destinies
are entwined.

499
01:00:10.520 --> 01:00:12.400
They're keeping you busy.

500
01:00:17.040 --> 01:00:19.040
I picked this up
in the kitchen.

501
01:00:19.120 --> 01:00:22.680
It's from the reception the other day.
I thought Mrs. Filipov might like it.

502
01:00:22.760 --> 01:00:26.520
Um, she will be thrilled.
That's very sweet of you.

503
01:00:27.600 --> 01:00:29.720
There's plenty more
if you're hungry.

504
01:00:31.120 --> 01:00:33.440
You're Jewish,
aren't you?

505
01:00:33.520 --> 01:00:37.680
There's nothing in our religion
that says you can't eat sturgeon.

506
01:00:37.760 --> 01:00:42.080
My father had a premonition
all this would happen.

507
01:00:42.160 --> 01:00:44.200
You mean the war?

508
01:00:44.280 --> 01:00:48.120
He understood that the hatred
of the jews ran deep.

509
01:00:48.200 --> 01:00:52.240
He was saving up to buy
some land in Palestine.

510
01:00:52.320 --> 01:00:56.360
He said it was the only land
we truly belonged in;

511
01:00:56.440 --> 01:00:59.200
the only land
we had a duty to defend.

512
01:00:59.280 --> 01:01:03.200
He insisted I learn
to use a rifle.

513
01:01:03.280 --> 01:01:05.440
I learned to shoot.

514
01:01:09.840 --> 01:01:14.760
I know that in times of war, personal
feelings should be put aside, but...

515
01:01:14.800 --> 01:01:16.800
I have a favor
to ask you.

516
01:01:16.880 --> 01:01:19.040
Of course.
Anything you want.

517
01:01:19.120 --> 01:01:22.120
I want to be reassigned.

518
01:01:24.160 --> 01:01:26.680
What's happened, Tania?

519
01:01:26.760 --> 01:01:29.080
@@@@@@

520
01:01:50.320 --> 01:01:52.200
He shot him.

521
01:01:55.880 --> 01:01:58.240
He shot him even though
he jumped first.

522
01:02:00.040 --> 01:02:02.000
Shot him on the run.

523
01:02:02.080 --> 01:02:04.240
It was
an impossible shot.

524
01:02:04.320 --> 01:02:06.520
I've never seen
anything like it.

525
01:02:06.600 --> 01:02:09.880
You've promised people
a victory I can't deliver.

526
01:02:11.880 --> 01:02:14.520
I don't stand a chance
against this man.

527
01:02:14.600 --> 01:02:16.600
You mustn't talk
like that, Vassili.

528
01:02:18.200 --> 01:02:21.680
What if I told you we found
a way to track his movements?

529
01:02:21.760 --> 01:02:23.800
We've got someone, Vassili.

530
01:02:23.880 --> 01:02:26.960
Someone close to him
passing us information.

531
01:02:27.040 --> 01:02:29.960
Next time you will be
one step ahead of him.

532
01:02:31.640 --> 01:02:33.480
I promise.

533
01:02:39.960 --> 01:02:42.480
@@

534
01:02:42.560 --> 01:02:46.000
Now I have a favor to ask.

535
01:02:46.080 --> 01:02:47.920
From me?

536
01:02:50.720 --> 01:02:52.560
It's about Tania.

537
01:02:57.840 --> 01:02:59.680
Come in.

538
01:03:04.480 --> 01:03:06.480
He doesn't even know you exist.

539
01:03:06.520 --> 01:03:10.160
But at that moment, you are closer
to him than anyone else on earth.

540
01:03:10.200 --> 01:03:13.240
You see his face
through the sight.

541
01:03:13.320 --> 01:03:15.600
You see whether he shaved
that morning or not.

542
01:03:15.640 --> 01:03:19.280
You can see whether he's married
by whether he has a wedding ring on.

543
01:03:21.640 --> 01:03:23.720
It's not like...

544
01:03:23.800 --> 01:03:26.880
just firing at a distant shape,
not just a uniform.

545
01:03:26.960 --> 01:03:29.880
It's a man's face.

546
01:03:29.960 --> 01:03:33.520
Those faces don't go away.

547
01:03:33.600 --> 01:03:38.560
They come back and they just-
they get replaced by more faces.

548
01:03:38.640 --> 01:03:41.680
Did Danilov ask you
to tell me this?

549
01:03:41.760 --> 01:03:45.360
He likes you very much. I think he'd try
anything to change your mind.

550
01:03:45.440 --> 01:03:48.080
Did he tell you
why I asked for the transfer?

551
01:03:48.160 --> 01:03:50.040
No.

552
01:03:50.080 --> 01:03:52.920
This morning, a list
arrived at headquarters.

553
01:03:52.960 --> 01:03:55.480
It was a list of civilians
who'd been...

554
01:03:55.560 --> 01:03:57.920
rounded up and sent to Germany
in a convoy...

555
01:03:58.000 --> 01:04:00.440
that left Stalingrad
three weeks ago.

556
01:04:02.040 --> 01:04:04.280
My parents
were amongst them.

557
01:04:06.520 --> 01:04:10.480
After 30 kilometers,
the German soldiers...

558
01:04:10.520 --> 01:04:14.480
stopped the train
and forced everyone out.

559
01:04:16.200 --> 01:04:20.560
In the middle of a bridge,
they bound them together,

560
01:04:20.600 --> 01:04:23.400
two by two.

561
01:04:23.480 --> 01:04:26.000
Mothers with daughters.

562
01:04:26.040 --> 01:04:27.920
Husbands and wives.

563
01:04:29.720 --> 01:04:33.800
They... Iined them up
against the railing,

564
01:04:33.880 --> 01:04:37.080
and then they fired
a single shot at each pair...

565
01:04:37.120 --> 01:04:39.000
to save bullets.

566
01:04:40.040 --> 01:04:42.680
It worked.

567
01:04:42.720 --> 01:04:47.120
The bodies of the ones who died
dragged the others under the water.

568
01:04:50.400 --> 01:04:52.440
I know they died together.

569
01:04:53.760 --> 01:04:56.440
They never would have let
themselves be separated.

570
01:05:11.200 --> 01:05:14.680
That's Koulikov's rifle.
It's a good... rifle.

571
01:05:23.520 --> 01:05:25.400
Thank you.

572
01:05:53.560 --> 01:05:56.160
I know how he leaves
the shelter.

573
01:05:56.240 --> 01:05:58.080
He goes through
the tractor factory.

574
01:05:58.160 --> 01:06:01.240
The tractor factory is big.

575
01:06:03.840 --> 01:06:06.440
I know exactly where.
He crawls through a gutter,

576
01:06:06.520 --> 01:06:09.280
under a grate
where the vats are,

577
01:06:09.360 --> 01:06:11.280
then he goes out
from the workshop.

578
01:06:11.360 --> 01:06:14.480
In between the two,
there's a place where he's in the open.

579
01:06:14.560 --> 01:06:17.280
It's under
a long, iron foot walk.

580
01:06:49.840 --> 01:06:51.800
Good luck, comrade.

581
01:08:32.560 --> 01:08:35.160
I know exactly where
he's waiting for me.

582
01:08:38.160 --> 01:08:40.920
He'll be on the foot walk
over the gutter.

583
01:08:41.000 --> 01:08:43.400
We'll take him out
from behind.

584
01:09:02.520 --> 01:09:07.520
We'll get to the other end
of the workshop through these pipes.

585
01:09:07.640 --> 01:09:09.480
Follow me.

586
01:10:50.760 --> 01:10:53.680
You go that way.
I'll go around this way.

587
01:10:53.760 --> 01:10:56.480
Okay?

588
01:11:11.520 --> 01:11:13.440
Shit!

589
01:11:20.520 --> 01:11:23.800
Sergei,
you should go back.

590
01:11:23.880 --> 01:11:26.960
- No, I'll be all right.
- Go back.

591
01:11:27.040 --> 01:11:29.280
No, you go!

592
01:11:33.640 --> 01:11:35.520
Keep your legs in.

593
01:12:16.640 --> 01:12:21.280
Come on. Come on. Come on.

594
01:13:17.440 --> 01:13:20.800
Comrade Stalin is asking for
one last effort!

595
01:13:20.880 --> 01:13:22.840
The fate of the motherland
is at risk!

596
01:13:22.920 --> 01:13:25.400
The fate of all those
you love and cherish!

597
01:13:25.480 --> 01:13:27.760
It's for them
that we fight today.

598
01:13:29.920 --> 01:13:33.360
Listen to me, Tania. The Germans
are throwing everything at us.

599
01:13:33.440 --> 01:13:36.240
If they're lucky, one in ten
of these soldiers will come back alive.

600
01:13:36.320 --> 01:13:39.160
You're highly educated.
You know languages.

601
01:13:39.240 --> 01:13:42.520
Every intercept you translate
saves hundreds of lives.

602
01:13:42.560 --> 01:13:46.280
Every message you decode
kills thousands of theirs.

603
01:13:46.320 --> 01:13:48.320
You have a duty to survive.

604
01:13:48.400 --> 01:13:50.880
Vassili was born to fire a gun.
It's what he knows.

605
01:13:50.920 --> 01:13:54.480
You and I were born
for a different purpose.

606
01:13:54.520 --> 01:13:57.280
If Vassili were here,
he would tell you the same thing.

607
01:14:00.400 --> 01:14:04.680
Where is he?
Where is Vassili?

608
01:15:07.920 --> 01:15:09.880
Keep your head down.

609
01:15:09.960 --> 01:15:12.480
- Tell me where he is.
- Stay into that pipe, Tania.

610
01:15:12.520 --> 01:15:14.480
Stay in. Stay in!
Get your head in!

611
01:15:22.000 --> 01:15:24.040
Slow down.

612
01:15:24.080 --> 01:15:26.000
Don't shoot.

613
01:15:30.800 --> 01:15:32.520
He's over there.

614
01:15:45.440 --> 01:15:48.320
Do you see the pillar
in front of you?

615
01:15:50.080 --> 01:15:52.480
I need you
to move round behind it.

616
01:16:01.960 --> 01:16:03.800
Go.

617
01:16:05.440 --> 01:16:10.560
Tania, I need you to find
a large piece of glass.

618
01:16:10.640 --> 01:16:13.680
Piece of glass.

619
01:16:15.160 --> 01:16:18.960
Do you see the kiln...

620
01:16:19.040 --> 01:16:22.640
behind me to the left
of the factory?

621
01:16:24.800 --> 01:16:26.640
Yes? I can't hear you.

622
01:16:26.760 --> 01:16:29.760
- Yes.
- Yes.

623
01:16:29.840 --> 01:16:32.000
Do you see...

624
01:16:32.040 --> 01:16:34.960
the two louvers?

625
01:16:36.240 --> 01:16:38.960
- Yes.
- Do you see the one...

626
01:16:39.040 --> 01:16:41.640
with a broken slat?

627
01:16:41.760 --> 01:16:43.520
Yes.

628
01:16:43.640 --> 01:16:45.640
This is what
I want you to do.

629
01:16:52.320 --> 01:16:55.440
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

630
01:16:55.520 --> 01:16:59.520
Three... two... one...

631
01:17:16.960 --> 01:17:19.480
Hello, Sacha.

632
01:17:25.360 --> 01:17:27.320
He was right
where you said he'd be.

633
01:17:28.840 --> 01:17:30.640
Nearly there.

634
01:17:33.800 --> 01:17:35.640
He's very clever.

635
01:17:40.640 --> 01:17:42.560
Tell me about him.

636
01:17:49.480 --> 01:17:53.160
Why was it his grandfather taught him
how to shoot and not his father?

637
01:17:53.280 --> 01:17:56.680
His father's dead.
His mother too.

638
01:17:59.520 --> 01:18:01.480
Does he talk
about his father?

639
01:18:01.520 --> 01:18:03.880
No. He didn't know him.

640
01:18:05.800 --> 01:18:08.000
Did he go to school?

641
01:18:08.040 --> 01:18:11.520
He knows how to write.
He answers lots of letters.

642
01:18:11.520 --> 01:18:14.520
Hmm. Is it girls
who write to him?

643
01:18:14.560 --> 01:18:17.280
Everyone writes to him.

644
01:18:17.320 --> 01:18:19.280
Is there a girl
he loves in his village?

645
01:18:19.360 --> 01:18:23.040
- Not in his village, here.
- Does she love him?

646
01:18:23.080 --> 01:18:25.960
Yes, because he's handsome.

647
01:18:26.040 --> 01:18:28.960
Because he's brave
and she's very beautiful.

648
01:18:29.040 --> 01:18:31.320
I know her well.
She's from my neighborhood.

649
01:18:31.400 --> 01:18:34.240
She went to the university.
They're handsome together.

650
01:18:34.320 --> 01:18:36.320
Later, the two of them
will get married.

651
01:18:42.080 --> 01:18:44.000
At least, I think so.

652
01:18:46.040 --> 01:18:48.960
And you, Sacha,

653
01:18:49.000 --> 01:18:50.880
why are you helping
the Germans?

654
01:18:54.760 --> 01:18:58.000
Because they're stronger.
Because they're going to win the war.

655
01:18:58.040 --> 01:19:01.160
And because you like
chocolate, huh?

656
01:19:03.240 --> 01:19:05.520
@@@@@@

657
01:19:17.080 --> 01:19:20.000
All these people here
know they're gonna die.

658
01:19:20.040 --> 01:19:23.240
So each night
when they make it back,

659
01:19:23.320 --> 01:19:25.920
- it's a bonus.

660
01:19:25.960 --> 01:19:28.480
- Excuse me.

661
01:19:28.520 --> 01:19:30.880
So, every cup of tea,

662
01:19:30.920 --> 01:19:33.040
every cigarette...

663
01:19:33.080 --> 01:19:36.520
becomes a little celebration.

664
01:19:36.560 --> 01:19:38.960
Because for a lot of us,
it maybe our last night.

665
01:19:40.480 --> 01:19:44.080
It's just something
you have to accept here.

666
01:19:44.160 --> 01:19:46.040
Everyone has their time.

667
01:19:50.160 --> 01:19:54.680
In the forest,
the wolf lives for three years,

668
01:19:54.760 --> 01:19:56.640
the donkey for nine.

669
01:19:59.640 --> 01:20:03.040
So, that's-that's got to be
a proverb from the Urals.

670
01:20:03.080 --> 01:20:05.040
It makes no sense to me
what's over.

671
01:20:05.080 --> 01:20:08.840
The donkey lives longer
because he's more useful.

672
01:20:08.920 --> 01:20:10.760
Makes absolute sense.

673
01:20:10.840 --> 01:20:12.840
There aren't any donkeys
in the forest.

674
01:20:12.920 --> 01:20:15.760
You made it up.

675
01:20:15.800 --> 01:20:19.520
So... I'm a donkey?

676
01:20:23.040 --> 01:20:26.160
People like you
and Danilov...

677
01:20:26.280 --> 01:20:28.080
have to survive this.

678
01:20:28.160 --> 01:20:31.400
People who have read books,
had an education.

679
01:20:32.880 --> 01:20:35.280
We'll need you
when the war is over.

680
01:20:35.320 --> 01:20:37.920
And if you survive?

681
01:20:38.000 --> 01:20:41.520
What will the useless
Vassili Zaitsev do then?

682
01:20:41.640 --> 01:20:44.680
I wanna work in a factory.

683
01:20:44.800 --> 01:20:49.080
My grand dad took me
to a factory once.

684
01:20:49.240 --> 01:20:54.000
There was this man there,
high up on a-

685
01:20:54.040 --> 01:20:56.400
on a foot walk.

686
01:20:56.440 --> 01:20:59.480
He wasn't wearing blue
like the others.

687
01:20:59.520 --> 01:21:03.560
The people he was supervising
didn't understand what they were doing.

688
01:21:03.640 --> 01:21:05.840
But for him,
for him up there,

689
01:21:05.920 --> 01:21:08.480
it was simple;
it was clear.

690
01:21:08.520 --> 01:21:13.520
And I thought, "One day,
I could be that man. "

691
01:21:18.960 --> 01:21:22.520
Sad to have a dream
you know won't happen.

692
01:21:24.240 --> 01:21:26.040
Why shouldn't it?

693
01:21:28.280 --> 01:21:30.080
You'll outlive us all.

694
01:21:30.160 --> 01:21:32.160
Hmm.

695
01:21:32.240 --> 01:21:35.080
You'll be the oldest donkey
in the forest.

696
01:21:51.360 --> 01:21:54.080
"150 meters stand between
the Germans and the Volga.

697
01:21:54.080 --> 01:21:56.480
"Today the whole world
is watching these 150meters.

698
01:21:56.520 --> 01:21:59.480
They are what makes
Stalingrad..."

699
01:21:59.520 --> 01:22:01.400
the capitol...

700
01:22:01.480 --> 01:22:03.560
of the war.

701
01:22:08.040 --> 01:22:09.920
Your friend, Tania...

702
01:22:11.280 --> 01:22:13.080
have you see her?

703
01:22:13.160 --> 01:22:15.840
She stays over there now,
with the snipers.

704
01:22:18.080 --> 01:22:20.800
Tell the major we're sending in
all of our sharp shooters...

705
01:22:20.880 --> 01:22:23.440
to support the attack
on the factory.

706
01:22:24.640 --> 01:22:27.000
Tell him Vassili
will be there.

707
01:26:08.640 --> 01:26:10.240
- I need to talk to you.
- Sure.

708
01:26:10.240 --> 01:26:11.080
- I need to talk to you.
- Sure.

709
01:26:15.080 --> 01:26:17.440
- Danilov.
- Hmm?

710
01:26:29.560 --> 01:26:32.040
You have to
stop writing about me.

711
01:26:35.320 --> 01:26:37.800
I'm not gonna get him
because I'm not good enough.

712
01:26:37.880 --> 01:26:41.560
Sooner or later, he's gonna find me,
he's gonna kill me.

713
01:26:41.640 --> 01:26:43.880
I've warned you before
not to talk like this.

714
01:26:45.880 --> 01:26:49.040
This time it's different.

715
01:26:50.560 --> 01:26:52.800
You've built me up...

716
01:26:52.880 --> 01:26:56.240
and up into someone I'm not.

717
01:26:57.600 --> 01:27:00.680
I can't carry that weight anymore.
I wanna fight.

718
01:27:01.800 --> 01:27:05.440
I want to fight just
as a regular soldier.

719
01:27:06.520 --> 01:27:08.360
I understand.

720
01:27:08.440 --> 01:27:12.000
The thing is, you're not a regular
soldier. You're extra ordinary.

721
01:27:12.040 --> 01:27:15.520
No, I'm what
you've made me.

722
01:27:15.600 --> 01:27:18.040
Nothing more.

723
01:27:22.120 --> 01:27:24.680
Why are you
telling me this now?

724
01:27:24.760 --> 01:27:27.000
Hmm? What's happened?

725
01:27:30.400 --> 01:27:32.240
What's changed?

726
01:27:37.000 --> 01:27:39.000
Did you speak
to Tania for me?

727
01:27:41.320 --> 01:27:43.160
- Yes.
- Well...

728
01:27:43.240 --> 01:27:45.520
will she reconsider?

729
01:27:49.040 --> 01:27:51.160
I don't know.

730
01:27:53.560 --> 01:27:57.280
She should. She'll be much safer.
She should, you know that.

731
01:27:57.320 --> 01:28:00.800
- Yeah.
- It'll be easier to get her reassigned.

732
01:28:00.840 --> 01:28:03.920
The Germans are preparing
another offensive in the city center.

733
01:28:04.000 --> 01:28:07.120
The propaganda battle is crucial
for morale. We need you more than ever.

734
01:28:07.200 --> 01:28:09.120
Sacha. Hold on. Sacha!

735
01:28:13.560 --> 01:28:16.360
- Tell him what you know, Sacha.
- Hello, Sacha.

736
01:28:16.440 --> 01:28:18.480
There was dust
on the major's boots.

737
01:28:18.560 --> 01:28:22.800
Sacha has the major convinced
he's gone over to the other side.

738
01:28:22.880 --> 01:28:25.760
I don't need to tell you
the risk she's taking.

739
01:28:25.800 --> 01:28:29.040
The dust was yellow. There's only
one place where there's dust like that-

740
01:28:29.120 --> 01:28:32.240
in the back of the chemical factory,
a big heap on the tracks.

741
01:28:34.120 --> 01:28:36.000
Well done.

742
01:28:36.040 --> 01:28:38.760
Sacha...

743
01:28:38.840 --> 01:28:41.160
wait for me outside then.

744
01:28:47.840 --> 01:28:49.440
- Danilov,
- Hmm?

745
01:28:49.480 --> 01:28:53.240
you had no right
to use him.

746
01:28:53.320 --> 01:28:56.320
No, no, I didn't use him,
Vassili.

747
01:28:56.400 --> 01:28:59.360
He did it of his own accord.

748
01:28:59.440 --> 01:29:01.840
You know why?

749
01:29:01.920 --> 01:29:03.920
Because he believes in you!

750
01:29:10.760 --> 01:29:14.240
Tomorrow morning, we're going
to take back the chemical factory.

751
01:29:14.320 --> 01:29:17.440
Sacha's informed the major
you'll be there,

752
01:29:17.480 --> 01:29:20.080
so now you know where
you have to wait for him.

753
01:29:20.160 --> 01:29:23.240
- In the middle of an assault.
- I'm following orders.

754
01:29:23.280 --> 01:29:25.360
I suggest you do the same.

755
01:29:27.040 --> 01:29:29.960
Now, I'm aware
of the risks.

756
01:29:30.040 --> 01:29:31.880
You'll be fine.

757
01:29:36.280 --> 01:29:38.120
Comrade.

758
01:30:03.520 --> 01:30:05.360
That's the Germans
up there.

759
01:30:05.440 --> 01:30:07.320
And yesterday
was the Russians.

760
01:30:07.400 --> 01:30:09.400
We're not very far now.

761
01:30:11.360 --> 01:30:13.960
Sacha...

762
01:30:14.040 --> 01:30:16.240
you're playing
a very dangerous game.

763
01:30:17.760 --> 01:30:19.760
I want you to win.

764
01:30:20.880 --> 01:30:24.000
See there?
Keep going along the river.

765
01:30:24.080 --> 01:30:26.600
It's safe... for a while.

766
01:34:31.240 --> 01:34:34.040
Aah!

767
01:34:53.880 --> 01:34:57.880
He's dead.
We found this on his corpse.

768
01:35:00.560 --> 01:35:04.120
Your reason for being here
has ceased to exist.

769
01:35:04.200 --> 01:35:06.240
Pardon me, Herr General,

770
01:35:06.320 --> 01:35:09.040
but I do not believe-

771
01:35:09.120 --> 01:35:11.320
There is a plane bound for Berlin
tomorrow evening.

772
01:35:11.360 --> 01:35:13.560
You will be on it.

773
01:35:16.400 --> 01:35:19.640
Until then, I must ask you
for your dog tags.

774
01:35:21.840 --> 01:35:24.800
Imagine how Russian propaganda
would profit from your death.

775
01:35:24.880 --> 01:35:27.160
If you fall,
you will fall unknown.

776
01:35:27.240 --> 01:35:29.520
You've already had
a near miss.

777
01:35:38.240 --> 01:35:41.160
Also please take
this War Merit Cross.

778
01:35:41.240 --> 01:35:42.640
It was awarded post humously...

779
01:35:42.720 --> 01:35:44.960
to a lieutenant of the 116th
Infantry Division...

780
01:35:45.040 --> 01:35:47.040
who fell here during the first days
of the battle.

781
01:35:47.040 --> 01:35:48.400
who fell here during the first days
of the battle.

782
01:35:49.560 --> 01:35:51.400
He was my son.

783
01:35:53.960 --> 01:35:56.760
If the landing is captured,
everything's lost!

784
01:35:59.160 --> 01:36:01.000
Come here.

785
01:36:04.160 --> 01:36:06.000
What did I tell you?

786
01:36:06.080 --> 01:36:08.600
You've been playing
your fiddle too much!

787
01:36:08.680 --> 01:36:11.320
If it's confirmed
that he's dead, we're sunk!

788
01:36:11.400 --> 01:36:14.960
- Well, you resunk.
- It isn't true.

789
01:36:15.040 --> 01:36:17.760
It was intercepted
from their staff headquarters.

790
01:36:17.800 --> 01:36:20.560
What do they have to do,
dangle his body in front our our men?

791
01:36:20.640 --> 01:36:23.480
They're lying.

792
01:36:23.560 --> 01:36:27.520
That's good.
Very good.

793
01:36:27.600 --> 01:36:31.240
Write it, then.
"Vassili Zaitsev is not dead.

794
01:36:31.320 --> 01:36:33.640
"This is what he had
for breakfast this morning.

795
01:36:33.720 --> 01:36:37.960
This is a picture of him reading
today's newspaper. " You're the poet.

796
01:36:38.040 --> 01:36:39.880
- What?

797
01:36:39.960 --> 01:36:42.400
You won't give up
the river bank!

798
01:36:42.480 --> 01:36:45.360
I don't care if you've lost
half your men!

799
01:36:45.440 --> 01:36:48.400
Lose the other half,
or lose yourself!

800
01:36:54.120 --> 01:36:56.400
Is he back?

801
01:36:58.440 --> 01:37:00.320
He should be back soon.

802
01:37:02.560 --> 01:37:04.840
The German attack cut the lines.
That's why he's late.

803
01:37:07.400 --> 01:37:09.280
Can we go outside?

804
01:37:15.400 --> 01:37:17.800
I wrote to my mother
about you.

805
01:37:17.880 --> 01:37:20.200
She wanted me to tell you
that once this war was over,

806
01:37:20.280 --> 01:37:22.560
if there's anything you needed-
anything at all-

807
01:37:22.600 --> 01:37:24.840
our family
will be there for you.

808
01:37:27.160 --> 01:37:29.160
You know I'm here for you.

809
01:37:33.400 --> 01:37:36.080
They're saying
Vassili is dead.

810
01:37:36.160 --> 01:37:40.320
Vassili Zaitsev
will never see his loved ones again.

811
01:37:40.360 --> 01:37:43.840
Surrender!
This is your only hope.

812
01:37:47.480 --> 01:37:50.000
You're upset.

813
01:37:50.080 --> 01:37:52.240
Because Zaitsev is dead?

814
01:37:55.080 --> 01:37:57.760
You don't have to hide it.
There's no shame in it.

815
01:37:58.760 --> 01:38:01.040
You're a Russian
like he is.

816
01:38:03.760 --> 01:38:05.840
Don't listen to them.

817
01:38:05.920 --> 01:38:09.040
It's just propaganda.

818
01:38:09.120 --> 01:38:11.080
He isn't dead.

819
01:38:12.200 --> 01:38:14.040
And do you know why?

820
01:38:15.240 --> 01:38:17.320
Because I haven't
killed him yet.

821
01:38:17.400 --> 01:38:20.200
@@@@@@

822
01:38:24.040 --> 01:38:25.920
I'm going to tell you
a little secret.

823
01:38:27.720 --> 01:38:30.640
Only you, because
I know I can trust you.

824
01:38:30.720 --> 01:38:33.760
But you must swear to me that
you won't tell another soul.

825
01:38:36.160 --> 01:38:39.000
You swear?

826
01:38:39.080 --> 01:38:42.000
I found a terrific spot.

827
01:38:42.080 --> 01:38:44.720
It's by the exit
from the train station.

828
01:38:44.800 --> 01:38:47.520
I'll hide
in the water tower.

829
01:38:47.600 --> 01:38:50.440
Tomorrow.
I'll wait for him there.

830
01:38:50.520 --> 01:38:54.400
You'll see.
He'll be there.

831
01:38:55.440 --> 01:38:59.440
He always is.

832
01:39:06.320 --> 01:39:09.960
I also want you to swear that from now
on, you'll stay home where you belong.

833
01:39:12.200 --> 01:39:15.720
Do you swear?
Yes?

834
01:39:18.680 --> 01:39:21.520
Good.

835
01:39:21.560 --> 01:39:23.480
"We know he's alive.
We know he won't fail us.

836
01:39:23.560 --> 01:39:26.720
We know because he is a part of us now.
Vassili is eternal. "

837
01:39:29.680 --> 01:39:32.960
Where have you been?
We've looked everywhere for you.

838
01:39:33.040 --> 01:39:36.520
Oh, didn't you hear?
I was dead.

839
01:39:36.600 --> 01:39:40.440
At least the noble sniper
Zaitsev...

840
01:39:42.480 --> 01:39:45.160
Vassili was dead.

841
01:39:45.240 --> 01:39:47.120
The real one.

842
01:39:49.400 --> 01:39:52.080
Me...

843
01:39:52.160 --> 01:39:54.000
I was asleep,

844
01:39:54.080 --> 01:39:55.920
and I missed my chance.

845
01:39:56.000 --> 01:40:01.120
Then, I was curled up
in a corner, hiding...

846
01:40:01.200 --> 01:40:03.560
from a man
who wants to kill me.

847
01:40:03.640 --> 01:40:06.320
I'll talk to Kruschev.

848
01:40:06.400 --> 01:40:09.320
He'll send you back
to your old division.

849
01:40:09.400 --> 01:40:12.600
- Where's Tania?
- She's at the shelter.

850
01:40:12.680 --> 01:40:14.840
I've been to the shelter.

851
01:40:14.920 --> 01:40:16.960
I told her you weren't dead.

852
01:40:18.640 --> 01:40:22.040
The major said so.
He said the other Germans were lying.

853
01:40:22.120 --> 01:40:25.080
He told me you were waiting
for him at the station.

854
01:40:28.840 --> 01:40:30.680
Vassili.

855
01:40:50.320 --> 01:40:52.160
Vassili.

856
01:40:53.640 --> 01:40:55.480
Vassili.

857
01:41:02.000 --> 01:41:04.240
My little Sacha.

858
01:41:04.280 --> 01:41:06.160
I knew it.

859
01:41:23.440 --> 01:41:26.000
- Vassili.
- Tania.

860
01:41:32.560 --> 01:41:34.720
I knew you weren't dead.

861
01:41:34.800 --> 01:41:37.120
How?

862
01:41:37.200 --> 01:41:39.840
Because we only just met.

863
01:41:43.360 --> 01:41:48.400
I prayed for the first time
since I was a little girl.

864
01:41:48.480 --> 01:41:51.640
When I opened my eyes,
Sacha was standing there...

865
01:41:51.720 --> 01:41:53.840
waiting to give me
the good news.

866
01:41:56.680 --> 01:41:59.520
I think he loves you
even more than I do.

867
01:42:22.920 --> 01:42:25.520
To the proper military authority,

868
01:42:25.560 --> 01:42:28.040
I'm calling to the commandant's
attention the recent changes noticed...

869
01:42:28.120 --> 01:42:32.000
in the attitude towards fighting
of soldier Vassili Zaitsev.

870
01:42:32.080 --> 01:42:36.000
He has attempted on several occasions
to escape his duties,

871
01:42:36.080 --> 01:42:38.360
voiced doubts on the chances
of our victory...

872
01:42:38.440 --> 01:42:40.280
and made defeatist comments
in public.

873
01:42:41.800 --> 01:42:44.320
The inexplicable
duration of his duel...

874
01:42:44.400 --> 01:42:49.080
with the Nazi sharpshooter
can only be explained by...

875
01:42:49.160 --> 01:42:51.840
his lack of belief
in the communist ideal.

876
01:42:59.480 --> 01:43:01.320
Good morning, Sacha.

877
01:43:03.200 --> 01:43:06.960
Once again, he knew
exactly where to find me.

878
01:43:07.000 --> 01:43:10.320
Don't you think
that's strange?

879
01:43:10.400 --> 01:43:14.040
- Apart from me, only you knew.

880
01:43:14.120 --> 01:43:16.760
I don't hold it against you,
Sacha.

881
01:43:16.840 --> 01:43:20.080
You've done
a very brave thing.

882
01:43:20.120 --> 01:43:23.000
You've chosen your camp.
I respect that.

883
01:43:23.040 --> 01:43:24.920
But it isn't my camp.

884
01:43:24.960 --> 01:43:27.760
We're both soldiers,

885
01:43:27.800 --> 01:43:32.360
and we're both enemies,
so I know you understand.

886
01:43:32.440 --> 01:43:37.800
I'm annoyed with you, little Sacha, for
not staying home as I made you swear to.

887
01:43:37.880 --> 01:43:41.080
I'm annoyed with you for obliging me
to do what I'm going to have to do.

888
01:43:46.400 --> 01:43:50.200
I've never seen anyone
frown so much in their sleep.

889
01:43:53.120 --> 01:43:55.520
How long have you been
watching me?

890
01:43:55.600 --> 01:43:57.880
All night.

891
01:43:57.960 --> 01:44:00.800
You've been snoring away
happily for hours.

892
01:44:00.880 --> 01:44:03.680
I don't snore.
Do I?

893
01:44:03.760 --> 01:44:05.600
Like a pig.

894
01:44:05.680 --> 01:44:08.080
I suppose I talk
in my sleep as well.

895
01:44:08.160 --> 01:44:10.040
Yes.

896
01:44:12.160 --> 01:44:14.120
There's something
I should tell you.

897
01:44:21.400 --> 01:44:24.120
On the train...

898
01:44:24.160 --> 01:44:26.040
coming here...

899
01:44:27.840 --> 01:44:29.840
we were in the same car.

900
01:44:29.920 --> 01:44:31.760
No.

901
01:44:31.840 --> 01:44:33.920
I saw you.

902
01:44:34.000 --> 01:44:37.320
You were reading,
and you fell asleep.

903
01:44:39.680 --> 01:44:43.120
I didn't dare look at you,
you were so beautiful.

904
01:44:44.800 --> 01:44:46.640
It was scary.

905
01:44:49.320 --> 01:44:53.280
Afterwards, I couldn't stop
thinking about you.

906
01:44:53.360 --> 01:44:55.200
It made me smile.

907
01:44:56.680 --> 01:45:00.880
And then I thought of all the men
who would get to hold you...

908
01:45:03.080 --> 01:45:05.080
who'd make you laugh...

909
01:45:07.520 --> 01:45:09.360
how lucky they were.

910
01:45:12.640 --> 01:45:13.920
And now I'm the one
lying next to you.

911
01:45:13.920 --> 01:45:15.640
And now I'm the one
lying next to you.

912
01:45:18.160 --> 01:45:21.000
- Was I snoring?
- Like a pig.

913
01:45:51.080 --> 01:45:53.680
- What?

914
01:45:57.240 --> 01:46:00.280
- Oh, my God!
- Oh, no.

915
01:46:00.360 --> 01:46:02.200
- Oh, my God!
- Tania, no.

916
01:46:02.280 --> 01:46:04.200
- Tania, no!
- No, get off me!

917
01:46:04.280 --> 01:46:06.800
- Get off me! Get off me!
- It's what he wants!

918
01:46:06.880 --> 01:46:08.760
- This is what he wants!
- Get off me!

919
01:46:08.800 --> 01:46:12.000
- No, he'll kill you. He'll kill you!
- Let me go!

920
01:46:12.080 --> 01:46:15.040
- I'll run after you, and he'll kill me.
- Let me go!

921
01:46:15.160 --> 01:46:17.840
- Let me go!
- This is what he wants! I'll get him.

922
01:46:17.880 --> 01:46:20.640
- I promise I'll get him.

923
01:46:20.720 --> 01:46:23.640
I'll get his rifle for you.
I promise, Tania.

924
01:46:42.040 --> 01:46:45.240
I need you.

925
01:46:48.320 --> 01:46:51.280
You have to leave now, Mrs. Filipov.
Stalingrad may fall.

926
01:46:51.360 --> 01:46:53.960
The last of the boats are leaving.
The Germans will be here any moment.

927
01:46:54.040 --> 01:46:57.240
He's brought you a pass.
You'll be safe on the other side.

928
01:46:57.320 --> 01:46:59.960
Gather your things, and we'll help you
carry them to the landing stage.

929
01:47:00.040 --> 01:47:03.480
I'm not leaving.
This is my home.

930
01:47:03.560 --> 01:47:06.440
This is my Sacha's home.
I can't leave.

931
01:47:06.520 --> 01:47:08.760
I have to tell you something,
Mrs. Filipov.

932
01:47:11.200 --> 01:47:14.080
Something very difficult
to understand.

933
01:47:14.160 --> 01:47:16.000
It's about Sacha.

934
01:47:29.880 --> 01:47:32.480
He's gone over to the Germans.
He's betrayed his country.

935
01:47:32.560 --> 01:47:34.840
He's with the enemy now.
He won't be coming back.

936
01:47:37.600 --> 01:47:39.480
Oh, my God.

937
01:47:42.320 --> 01:47:44.160
Oh, my God.

938
01:47:46.960 --> 01:47:50.040
He's become a traitor.

939
01:47:50.120 --> 01:47:52.880
The poor little thing.

940
01:47:52.960 --> 01:47:55.680
What has he done?

941
01:47:58.320 --> 01:48:00.280
So, he's going to
stay over there?

942
01:48:05.600 --> 01:48:10.240
Yes... he's going to
stay over there.

943
01:48:10.280 --> 01:48:13.840
I shouldn't
be saying this, comrade Commissar,

944
01:48:13.920 --> 01:48:16.640
but maybe
it's for the best.

945
01:48:16.720 --> 01:48:19.000
If the Germans have won,
he'll be safe.

946
01:48:19.040 --> 01:48:22.800
I know it's wrong, but perhaps
he has made the right choice.

947
01:48:41.280 --> 01:48:44.040
- Oh! Oh, Tania!
- Tania?

948
01:48:45.160 --> 01:48:47.840
- Oh, Tania!
- Tania!

949
01:48:48.840 --> 01:48:51.680
Oh, my God! Oh!

950
01:49:07.280 --> 01:49:11.800
I need a doctor!
A doctor!

951
01:49:15.400 --> 01:49:18.080
I have a pass.
I have a pass!

952
01:49:18.160 --> 01:49:20.000
You must let her cross.

953
01:49:22.600 --> 01:49:24.480
Please!

954
01:49:24.520 --> 01:49:28.440
- It's useless. She'll never make it.
- No! No, she will!

955
01:49:28.480 --> 01:49:31.480
She's my daughter!
She's my daughter!

956
01:49:31.520 --> 01:49:33.880
- I beg of you!
- All right.

957
01:49:33.960 --> 01:49:36.640
- Oh, thank you!
- Put this one on the boat.

958
01:50:21.600 --> 01:50:24.160
Where is he?

959
01:50:24.200 --> 01:50:26.640
Where's the major?

960
01:50:26.720 --> 01:50:28.800
A few inches
from your face.

961
01:50:31.520 --> 01:50:34.360
I've been such a fool,
Vassili.

962
01:50:34.440 --> 01:50:38.520
Man will always be man.

963
01:50:38.600 --> 01:50:40.600
There is no new man.

964
01:50:41.840 --> 01:50:45.080
We tried so hard to create
a society that was equal,

965
01:50:45.160 --> 01:50:47.800
where there'd be nothing
to envy your neighbor.

966
01:50:47.880 --> 01:50:51.080
But there's always
something to envy.

967
01:50:52.680 --> 01:50:54.680
A smile...

968
01:50:54.760 --> 01:50:56.600
a friendship.

969
01:50:58.040 --> 01:51:01.920
Something you don't have
and want to appropriate.

970
01:51:01.960 --> 01:51:05.440
In this world-
even a Soviet one-

971
01:51:05.480 --> 01:51:08.520
there will always
be rich and poor.

972
01:51:10.240 --> 01:51:12.240
Rich in gifts...

973
01:51:13.640 --> 01:51:15.520
poor in gifts.

974
01:51:16.520 --> 01:51:18.400
Rich in love...

975
01:51:19.560 --> 01:51:21.400
poor in love.

976
01:51:27.440 --> 01:51:30.400
Tania isn't coming back.

977
01:51:30.440 --> 01:51:33.320
She's dead, Vassili.

978
01:51:41.640 --> 01:51:45.720
She was cut down by shrapnel.
It was quick.

979
01:51:45.800 --> 01:51:47.680
I don't think
she even saw it coming.

980
01:51:49.400 --> 01:51:51.360
She was on her way
back to you.

981
01:51:51.400 --> 01:51:56.320
As soon as she had seen Mrs. Filipov to
the boats, she was coming back for you.

982
01:51:56.360 --> 01:52:01.000
She was right.
You're a good man, Vassili.

983
01:52:05.000 --> 01:52:07.440
I want to help you,
Vassili.

984
01:52:07.520 --> 01:52:10.080
Let me do one last thing.

985
01:52:10.120 --> 01:52:12.520
Something useful
for a change.

986
01:52:17.880 --> 01:52:19.760
Let me show you
where the major is.

987
01:52:19.840 --> 01:52:22.200
Don't do that.
Don't do that!

988
01:56:26.440 --> 01:56:31.440
Today, February3, 1943,
is an ominous day for Hitler...

989
01:56:31.480 --> 01:56:35.720
and the endless columns of hundreds
of thousands of German prisoners.

990
01:56:35.840 --> 01:56:39.520
It is an unforgettable day
of hope for our motherland.

991
01:56:39.600 --> 01:56:42.880
-@@@@@@

992
01:56:51.880 --> 01:56:55.720
After 180days of heroic combat...

993
01:56:55.800 --> 01:56:57.800
in the market city
of Stalingrad,

994
01:56:57.840 --> 01:57:02.880
and as a result of the valor
and self-sacrifice of our soldiers,

995
01:57:02.960 --> 01:57:05.960
the commander
of our glorious Red Army...

996
01:57:06.000 --> 01:57:09.040
received
the unconditional surrender...

997
01:57:09.120 --> 01:57:12.680
of the German fascist invaders.

998
01:57:24.360 --> 01:57:28.400
Sorry. No, young man,
I cannot find...

999
01:57:28.480 --> 01:57:30.320
